# Default loop

This project's loop is the four RRR skills. They are the source of truth. Do not merge them
into a generic Gauntlet / prompt-writer loop. Role walls are the point.

| Phase | Skill | Job |
|---|---|---|
| Decide | `rrr-slice` | Write a decided plan (`docs/slices/task-*.md`). Presentation, grounding, exposure. |
| Build | `rrr-pipeline` | Execute that plan. GPU-baked GLSL + harness. Ceiling is **PASS**. |
| Judge pixels | `rrr-critique` | Hostile art director. Blind A/B, fresh overlay. Only this role may award **WOWED**. |
| Judge feel | `rrr-playcritique` | Drive a real Playwright session. Do not score art. |

`GAUNTLET.md` is the roll-out order. It wires the first three skills; it is not a substitute
for them.

## Session start

Read `HANDOFF.md` first. For the Jackbox party game, `docs/design/party-loop.md` wins if it
disagrees with HANDOFF or gameplay-plan.

## Hard rules

- A builder never grades its own fix. Re-critique after every build.
- Never contaminate a critic with "this is fixed" — only what was *claimed*.
- One owner per coupled concern; run sequentially.
- Use `npm run build`, never `npx vite build`.
